id:                     E378
trigger_tool: conan
phase: source
error_signature: Calling source\(\) in .*archives.*|conan source.*unrecognized arguments.*output-folder
severity: 2
category:               platform, conan2, source-folder, worktree-contamination
match_keywords: conan source, source_folder, output-folder, absolute recipe path, strip_root
title: Run Conan source probes only from an isolated recipe copy
root_cause: Conan 2.29.1 does not accept conan source --output-folder and an absolute recipe path still sets source_folder to the recipe directory, so get(strip_root=True) extracts into the worktree.
affected_scope: Conan 2.29.1 source-method tests for recipes whose source() extracts archives at the source folder root.
verification_cmd: Copy only conanfile.py and conandata.yml to a create-new isolated recipe directory, run conan source . there, and verify the original worktree status is unchanged.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: isolated-recipe-copy-source-probe
rec_description: Treat the current recipe directory as the source output of conan source, so every source probe must execute from a disposable isolated recipe copy.
rec_command: Create a new evidence/case/recipe directory, copy the recipe metadata, run conan source . with a case-local Conan home, and compare the original worktree before and after.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-source-isolated-copy
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach:
fallback_description:
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern: conan source .*--output-folder|conan source [A-Z]:.*archives
forbid_1_reason: The unsupported option fails before source(), while an absolute worktree recipe path still writes extracted source into that recipe directory.
forbid_1_consequence: Large upstream trees contaminate the candidate worktree and can overlap intended recipe files.
principles:
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
